IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il46-nouns`
IMPORT `il46-cross-references`

-- Row il-46. The sound citations point at what their citing words say, and the recorded facts about the defects and the controls are what NOTES.md says they are.
-- The defects themselves are NOT asserted sound anywhere in this file: their failing assertions are in il46-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in il46-cross-references.l4, not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of the sound citations`

-- The four controls point at what they say.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 14(ב)(2)(א) to NII chapter ה׳, the injury allowance`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 14(ב)(2)(ג) to NII chapter ג׳, the maternity benefits`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 1 of the 1999 Order to NII Schedule י״א, the quarter`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 14(ז) to NII s 351(ז1), a person determined to be missing`)
-- Each control's target is printed under the name the citing words use.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 14(ב)(2)(א) to NII chapter ה׳, the injury allowance`)'s `the target is printed under the name the citing words use in the consolidation` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`reference: s 14(ב)(2)(ג) to NII chapter ג׳, the maternity benefits`)'s `the target is printed under the name the citing words use in the consolidation` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`reference: s 1 of the 1999 Order to NII Schedule י״א, the quarter`)'s `the target is printed under the name the citing words use in the consolidation` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`reference: s 14(ז) to NII s 351(ז1), a person determined to be missing`)'s `the target is printed under the name the citing words use in the consolidation` EQUALS TRUE

§ `Tests of what was read from where`

-- Only the control in s 14(ז) has both limbs read from an official page; it is the one page that wrote the citing words and the target.
#ASSERT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 14(ז) to NII s 351(ז1), a person determined to be missing`)
-- No other record has both limbs official: the defects rest in part on a consolidation or on a later change that is not ruled out, and the other controls on the consolidations alone.
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: reg 1(א) of the Reduced Rates Regulations to s 1 of the 1999 Order, the reduced amount`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 14(ו1) to NII s 341, the reduced amount determined under that section`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: reg 1 of the Special Provisions Regulations to NII chapter ג׳, the injury allowance`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: reg 1(4)(ב) of the Exemption Regulations to NII chapter ו2, the disability pension`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 14(ב)(2)(א) to NII chapter ה׳, the injury allowance`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 14(ב)(2)(ג) to NII chapter ג׳, the maternity benefits`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 1 of the 1999 Order to NII Schedule י״א, the quarter`))
-- P1 limb (a) is official; P2 limb (a) is mixed; P3 limb (a) is the consolidation only.
#ASSERT (`reference: reg 1(א) of the Reduced Rates Regulations to s 1 of the 1999 Order, the reduced amount`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 14(ו1) to NII s 341, the reduced amount determined under that section`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument for one part and the consolidation only for another`
#ASSERT (`reference: reg 1 of the Special Provisions Regulations to NII chapter ג׳, the injury allowance`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: reg 1(4)(ב) of the Exemption Regulations to NII chapter ו2, the disability pension`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`

§ `Tests of what the two descriptions of each defect say`

-- What the citing words say it points at, and what the target is, as the texts show them. Each is a statement of the difference; none says the difference does not matter.
#ASSERT (`reference: reg 1(א) of the Reduced Rates Regulations to s 1 of the 1999 Order, the reduced amount`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `the meaning of the term for the reduced amount`
#ASSERT (`reference: reg 1(א) of the Reduced Rates Regulations to s 1 of the 1999 Order, the reduced amount`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `a provision that fixes a sum by the average wage of the first month of a quarter`
#ASSERT (`reference: reg 1(א) of the Reduced Rates Regulations to s 1 of the 1999 Order, the reduced amount`)'s `the target is printed under the name the citing words use in the consolidation` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT (`reference: s 14(ו1) to NII s 341, the reduced amount determined under that section`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `the provision that fixes the reduced amount`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 14(ו1) to NII s 341, the reduced amount determined under that section`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `a power to fix a sum by order, with the reduced collection threshold defined in another section`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 14(ו1) to NII s 341, the reduced amount determined under that section`)'s `the target is printed under the name the citing words use in the consolidation` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT (`reference: reg 1 of the Special Provisions Regulations to NII chapter ג׳, the injury allowance`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `the chapter on maternity insurance`
#ASSERT (`reference: reg 1 of the Special Provisions Regulations to NII chapter ג׳, the injury allowance`)'s `the target is printed under the name the citing words use in the consolidation` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`reference: reg 1(4)(ב) of the Exemption Regulations to NII chapter ו2, the disability pension`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `no chapter by that name in the consolidation`

§ `Tests of the 1968 numbering`

-- Read in the 1968 numbering, each of the two chapter citations in the regulations points at what its citing words say; that is what the concordance table in the consolidation shows (old ג׳ to ה׳, old ו׳2 to ט׳).
-- Whether that is how the letters came to be as they are is an inference, and is not asserted here (fork F3 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says under the 1968 numbering` (`reference: reg 1 of the Special Provisions Regulations to NII chapter ג׳, the injury allowance`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says under the 1968 numbering` (`reference: reg 1(4)(ב) of the Exemption Regulations to NII chapter ו2, the disability pension`)
-- The question was not asked of the other records, so the answer is "no" for them by construction.
#ASSERT (NOT `the citation points at what it says under the 1968 numbering` (`reference: s 14(ב)(2)(ג) to NII chapter ג׳, the maternity benefits`))

§ `Tests of the change of version`

-- Sefer HaChukim 1607 p. 22 (7 January 1997 = 28 Tevet 5757): the Law's definition of the National Insurance Law moves from the 1968 version to the 1995 version.
#ASSERT (`change: the Law's definition of the National Insurance Law moved from the 1968 version to the 1995 version`)'s `it was published on` EQUALS Date 7 1 1997
#ASSERT (`change: the Law's definition of the National Insurance Law moved from the 1968 version to the 1995 version`)'s `the regulations in question were published on` EQUALS Date 12 1 1995
#ASSERT (`change: the Law's definition of the National Insurance Law moved from the 1968 version to the 1995 version`)'s `the version named before` EQUALS "the 1968 version"
#ASSERT (`change: the Law's definition of the National Insurance Law moved from the 1968 version to the 1995 version`)'s `the version named after` EQUALS "the 1995 version"
#ASSERT `the change was published on or after the day the regulations were published` (`change: the Law's definition of the National Insurance Law moved from the 1968 version to the 1995 version`)

§ `Tests of the date pairs`

-- The control, the pair that Sefer HaChukim 1798 p. 433, s 1(1), replaces: one day, 1 March 1999, by both dates; the consolidation no longer prints it.
#ASSERT `the two dates name the same day` (`date pair: the instruction replaces 13 Adar 5759 and 1 March 1999, which name one day`)
#ASSERT (`date pair: the instruction replaces 13 Adar 5759 and 1 March 1999, which name one day`)'s `the Hebrew date names` EQUALS Date 1 3 1999
#ASSERT (`date pair: the instruction replaces 13 Adar 5759 and 1 March 1999, which name one day`)'s `the Gregorian date names` EQUALS Date 1 3 1999
#ASSERT (`date pair: the instruction replaces 13 Adar 5759 and 1 March 1999, which name one day`)'s `the consolidation prints the same pair` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT (`date pair: the instruction replaces 13 Adar 5759 and 1 March 1999, which name one day`)'s `read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
-- The pair the instruction inserts: 14 Adar 5761 is 9 March 2001 and 1 March 2001 is 6 Adar 5761, a difference of eight days; the consolidation repeats the pair.
#ASSERT (`date pair: the instruction gives 14 Adar 5761 and 1 March 2001 for one day`)'s `the Hebrew date names` EQUALS Date 9 3 2001
#ASSERT (`date pair: the instruction gives 14 Adar 5761 and 1 March 2001 for one day`)'s `the Gregorian date names` EQUALS Date 1 3 2001
#ASSERT `the Hebrew date falls after the Gregorian date` (`date pair: the instruction gives 14 Adar 5761 and 1 March 2001 for one day`)
#ASSERT (NOT `the two dates name the same day` (`date pair: the instruction gives 14 Adar 5761 and 1 March 2001 for one day`))
#ASSERT (`date pair: the instruction gives 14 Adar 5761 and 1 March 2001 for one day`)'s `the consolidation prints the same pair` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`date pair: the instruction gives 14 Adar 5761 and 1 March 2001 for one day`)'s `read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
